1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From granddaughter Karin - 
2 CONT
2 CONT My Grandpa Einar was maried with Tala.  She was one of 3 daughters, and came from a relatively rich family at Sævelandsvik, close to Akrehamn.  They inherited some fishing factories, and in addition Einar bought two to three fishi
2 CONC ng boats.
2 CONT
2 CONT Einar was major in Åkra for 12 years.  In additiion he was front figure in the fishing organizations over the whole country.  He was the head leader of something called Norges fiskarlag, which is an organization taking care of the
2 CONC  fisherman's interests.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also the leader of the financial bank system, who decided which company should get loans from the bank.  He had a great influence on the economic life for the fishermen in those days.  He worked close up to the parliament a
2 CONC nd the government, and had a huge position in those days when fishing activities were the most important income in our country.
